        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T18:03:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given what I suggested above, you can simplify this as:\n\n```\nstruct mod_plt_sec *mod_plt;\n\n...\n\nmod_plt \u003d !str_has_prefix(secstrings + dstsec-\u003esh_name, \".init\") ? \u0026mod-\u003earch.core : \u0026mod-\u003earch.init;\n\nplt_count \u003d count_plts(syms, rels, numrels, sechds[i].sh_info, dstsec, \u0026mod_plt-\u003eelf64_rela_rht);\nif (plt_count \u003c 0)\n        goto free_and_destroy_rht;\n        \nmod_plt-\u003eplt_max_entries +\u003d plt_count;\n```\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "revId": "139b4cde28acd00c07ed864f0ef6b0f69756e518",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43a83446_8afbc0d8",
