      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T18:03:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I checked and this seems to be called when the module is unloaded or as part of error handling while loading the module, but not in the case that the module is loaded successfully, so the hashtables will still be allocated and populated after the module loads, despite not needing them.\n\nI believe `module_arch_freeing_init` does get called in case we successfully load the module though, along with the case where the module is unloaded or in case of an error when loading the module. Maybe we should define that here instead?",
      "revId": "139b4cde28acd00c07ed864f0ef6b0f69756e518",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
